{"id": "SCGAI-001", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "A prompt is not merely written; it is socially constructed."}
{"id": "SCGAI-002", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt ownership can turn into collaboration after the copied prompt produces a difference."}
{"id": "SCGAI-003", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Collaborative prompting makes the history of modification part of the creative object."}
{"id": "SCGAI-004", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt communities conduct experiments where the literature has not yet stabilized."}
{"id": "SCGAI-005", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "A prompt can be published not to generate an image but to generate behavior in other people."}
{"id": "SCGAI-006", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt sharing is described as feeding an ecosystem that feeds the prompter."}
{"id": "SCGAI-007", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The paper demotes prompt engineering from an individual technical skill to a socio-technical practice."}
{"id": "SCGAI-008", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt provenance may change whether users are willing to enter collaboration at all."}
{"id": "SCGAI-005-A", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The prompt feed may be a stigmergic field: strangers can coordinate through traces without ever collaborating directly."}
{"id": "SCGAI-004-A", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Some prompts may be epistemic actions: their real output is knowledge about the machine."}
{"id": "SCGAI-004-B", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt engineering may be adaptive folk theorization: a successful rule can become false while its words remain unchanged."}
{"id": "SCGAI-003-A", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt history may not record the cognition; it may be part of the cognition."}
{"id": "SCGAI-008-A", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompts could acquire patina: provenance can be made to look like wear on a tool."}
{"id": "SCGAI-006-A", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The prompt commons may not oppose private ownership; private benefit and collective revelation can be the same innovation process."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-01", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The user no longer writes the prompt that actually runs."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-02", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The prompt has crossed the line from prose artifact to versioned software artifact."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-03", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "A sufficiently comprehensive prompt becomes an attractive nuisance."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-04", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Long prompt work survives by leaving spoor outside the conversation."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-05", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompting can occur without words: preference itself is becoming executable."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-06", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The prompt writer can disappear one level upward and write only the conditions from which prompts are generated."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-07", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Memory becomes more controllable when it is given a name the model must carry."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-08", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The position of words now has an economic physics."}
{"id": "WWP-20260817-09", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "A prompt can become obsolete while remaining perfectly preserved."}
{"id": "FIELD-20260817-01", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The minimal reproducible prompt is a receipt for an execution event, not a string."}
{"id": "FIELD-20260817-02", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt expertise is migrating from phrasing toward environment design, tests, and evaluative judgment."}
{"id": "FIELD-20260817-03", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "The archive and the active prompt must diverge: remember everything, load selectively."}
{"id": "FIELD-20260817-04", "type": "ZETTEL", "title": "Prompt lineage is an epistemic apparatus, not merely an authorship ledger."}
